  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV SDN - Sudan (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan, HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Sudan)This program has the following goals: To halt the further spread of HIV among the Sudanese population and maintain HIV prevalence rates below 2.5% among all most-at-risk populations and below 0.3% among the general population by 2017.  To improve the quality of life, health and wellbeing of people living with HIV by providing universal access to comprehensive quality HIV treatment, care and support services. The objectives of this program are: HIV PREVENTION AMONG KEY AND VULNERABLE POPULATIONS: HIV TRANSMISSION AMONG KEY AND VULNERABLE POPULATIONS&apos; SEXUAL NETWORKS REDUCED THROUGH INCREASING THEIR ACCESS AND UTILIZATION OF HIV PREVENTION SERVICES.  HIV PREVENTION AMONG THE GENERAL POPULATION TO SCALE UP AND IMPROVE THE QUALITY OF KEY HIV-PREVENTION PROGRAMMES AND SERVICES FOR THE GENERAL POPULATION.  IMPROVING ACCESS TO HIV SERVICES IN HUMANITARIAN SETTING.  POSITIVE HEALTH, DIGNITY AND PREVENTION FOR PLHIV.  STRENGTHENING ACCESS AND QUALITY OF TREATMENT, CARE AND SUPPORT FOR PEOPLE LIVING WITH HIV (PLHIV): TO INCREASE ART COVERAGE AND IMPROVE QUALITY OF TREATMENT SERVICES.  STRENGTHENING LEADERSHIP, GOVERNANCE AND COORDINATION OF THE HIV RESPONSE.  STRENGTHENING STRATEGIC INFORMATION SYSTEMS: EFFECTIVE AVAILABILITY, SHARING AND UTILISATION OF STRATEGIC INFORMATION ON HIV/AIDS TO GUIDE THE IMPLEMENTATION OF EVIDENCE-INFORMED POLICIES, PROGRAMMES AND SERVICES.  SUPPORTIVE POLICY, LEGAL AND SOCIAL ENVIRONMENTS FOR A MULTISECTORAL RESPONSE TO HIV AND AIDS</narrative>
  </description>
